From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:32:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 67/70] renderer: draw a frame's image quads from one buffer

Every image placement created a GPU buffer for its one quad on every
frame and released it after the draw: with a few dozen placements at a
display's 120-144 Hz, thousands of buffer allocations a second, which
showed in macOS samples as newBufferWithBytes in the driver.

The quads of every placement are now built once per frame (State.prepare)
into one buffer each frame in flight holds, like its cells, and each
placement is one instanced draw at its first quad (base instance), its
backdrop's bleed quads included. Base instances need
glDrawArraysInstancedBaseInstance (OpenGL 4.2; Ghostty asks for 4.3) and
drawPrimitives:...:baseInstance: on Metal.
